d 'SURADF': module to conduct series-specific SUR-ADF panel unit root test
d
d  suradf implements the series-specific panel unit root test of
d Breuer, McNown and Wallace (2002, Oxford Bulletin of Economics
d and Statistics 64(5), 527-546, doi:10.1111/1468-0084.00276).
d Conventional panel unit root tests - Levin-Lin, Im-Pesaran-Shin,
d Maddala-Wu, and the multivariate ADF of Sarno and Taylor
d implemented in your madfuller - test a joint hypothesis. When
d they reject, the user learns only that at least one series in the
d panel is stationary, with no indication of how many or which.
d suradf instead estimates the N augmented Dickey-Fuller equations
d as a system of seemingly unrelated regressions, with lag orders
d free to differ across members and errors contemporaneously
d correlated across them, and tests the unit root null separately
d for each member. The output names which series are I(0) and which
d are I(1). Because the null distribution depends on the estimated
d covariance matrix of the system, no tabulated critical values
d apply; the paper is explicit that its own values "cannot be
d applied directly to other data sets". suradf therefore simulates
d series-specific critical values for the panel at hand, following
d the procedure in Section V of the paper. 
d
d KW: panel data
d KW: unit root
d KW: SUF-ADF
d
d Requires: Stata version 14
d
d Distribution-Date: 20261011
d
d Author:   Merwan Roudane, NA
d Support: email  merwanroudane920@@gmail.com
d
f suradf.ado
f suradf.sthlp
f suradf_asean6.do
f suradf_asean6.dta
f suradf_example.do
f suradf_methods.sthlp
